  "decisions": [
    "Interpreter distribution identities/qualification belong to the same authenticated catalog as SDK releases; old archives omit the optional interpreters field.",
    "Fixed astral-sh/python-build-standalone release asset naming, pinned archive/executable/materialized-tree identities and bounded native parsing; no downloaded adapters/install scripts/pip/system writes.",
    "Safe internal file aliases are materialized as protected independent files. External/directory/dangling/cyclic aliases, ambiguous metadata records, unsafe paths and extra gzip/tar data refuse.",
    "Private root identity, canonical ownership, all file hashes/modes/single-link reads and exact counts/bytes are checked before use and after stopped SDK qualification.",
    "SDK shutdown permanently revokes its own cancellation scope; the independent preparer performs the final integrity check without clearing/reviving the SDK signal.",
    "The maintainer generator drafts exact future interpreter entries from explicit approved release metadata and bytes; it does not fetch, execute, install, qualify or publish."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Both SDK and interpreter catalog entries remain upstream_only. Source-build proof is not installed/frozen or cross-platform qualification.",
    "Durable interpreter setup/discovery, native pinned acquisition/cache/recovery integration and authenticated managed-interpreter publication are still pending.",
    "Managed SDK identities/receipts must bind the full private interpreter build/tree, not just executable SHA; retain historical slot/record compatibility. Do not relabel external registration as managed setup.",
    "User-facing CLI/HTTP/Versions UI, update policy and full P5-P10 data/switch/rollback/authority/crash/performance/approval/package acceptance remain.",
    "The current-continuity test uses final0.14.1 on CPython3.14.7, not original b47380 or a newer CIGAR release. The later real build here is CPython, not the SDK.",
    "Production remote catalog hosting/trust, durable withdrawal integration and genuine newer approved SDK artifacts remain explicit prerequisites where required."
  ],
  "development_notes": [
    "The first maintainer example completed SDK checks but treated normal SDK-close cancellation as preparer cancellation during the final tree audit. Separate scopes fixed it; no old signal was reset.",
    "A web extraction of tag metadata was inconsistent; exact official API bytes and downloaded artifact digest/length were verified directly before native execution.",
    "All33 native tests passed initially, but a recorder checked an obsolete hardcoded test-image suffix after the tar dependency changed Cargo unit hashes. The completed log was resolved to its actual Cargo-reported image and matched to both in-process digests without replaying SDK effects."
  ],
